    dict(key='07-mode-digits', kind='figure', title='How a file mode is read',
         body='mode_digits',
         narration="Let's see the core idea on two real files. [[slnc 400]] A mode has four digits. [[slnc 300]] The first holds the special bits. [[slnc 300]] Then one digit for the owner, one for the group, and one for everyone else. [[slnc 300]] In each digit, read is four, write is two, and execute is one, added together. [[slnc 700]] On the left, the hidden shell in the temp folder: four seven five five. [[slnc 300]] The four is the set user id bit. [[slnc 300]] Seven is read, write and execute for the owner, and five is read and execute for the rest. [[slnc 300]] So anyone can run it, and it runs as root. [[slnc 300]] It is not on the allow-list. [[slnc 700]] On the right, the shadow file, which holds the password hashes: zero six four four. [[slnc 300]] The last four means everyone can read it. [[slnc 300]] The policy allows at most zero six four zero."),
    dict(key='08-act-1-figure', kind='figure', title='Twenty findings, and the seven a machine can fix',
         body='report_grid',
         narration="First demo: the shop's server image, before any fix. [[slnc 400]] Here is the report: twenty findings, worst first. [[slnc 300]] Red ones are critical or high, amber ones are medium, and grey ones are low. [[slnc 700]] A second root account called toor. [[slnc 300]] A test account with no password. [[slnc 300]] Telnet, the Docker A P I and Redis, listening on every interface. [[slnc 300]] And a copy of a shell with the set user id bit, in the temp folder. [[slnc 700]] Seven boxes have a green border. [[slnc 300]] They are file permissions, and a machine can fix them safely. [[slnc 300]] The other thirteen are accounts, S S H settings, kernel settings and ports. [[slnc 300]] Those need a person to decide."),
    dict(key='09-act-1-1', kind='console', title="Act One — The shop's server image, before any fix",
         body="ONE. The shop's server image, before any fix.\n  HOW A MODE IS READ, DIGIT BY DIGIT:\n    file     /tmp/.hidden-shell   /etc/shadow\n    mode     4755                 0644\n    special  4 set-user-id        0 none\n    user     7 rwx                6 rw-\n    group    5 r-x                4 r--\n    other    5 r-x                4 r--\n    policy   not allowed          at most 0640",
         narration='Here is the real output. [[slnc 400]] First, two modes, read digit by digit. [[slnc 300]] The hidden shell is four seven five five. [[slnc 300]] The four is the set user id bit, and seven, five, five give read, write and execute to the owner, and read and execute to everyone else. [[slnc 300]] The shadow file is zero six four four, so everyone can read it, and the policy allows at most zero six four zero.'),
    dict(key='10-act-1-2', kind='console', title="Act One — The shop's server image, before any fix",
         body='ONE. (continued)\n  THE REPORT: 20 FINDINGS, WORST FIRST (auto = a machine can fix):\n    CRITICAL empty-password      test\n    CRITICAL extra-root-account  toor\n    CRITICAL open-port           port 23\n    CRITICAL open-port           port 2375\n    CRITICAL open-port           port 6379\n    CRITICAL ssh-empty-passwords /etc/ssh/sshd_config\n    CRITICAL unexpected-setuid   /tmp/.hidden-shell  auto\n    HIGH     cron-group-writable /etc/cron.daily/backup.sh  auto\n    HIGH     default-account     test\n    HIGH     loose-permissions   /etc/shadow  auto\n    HIGH     loose-permissions   /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key  auto\n    HIGH     loose-permissions   /opt/app/config.properties  auto',
         narration='The report, worst first. [[slnc 300]] Seven critical findings: an empty password, a second root, three open ports, empty passwords allowed in S S H, and the set user id shell. [[slnc 300]] The word auto marks a finding that a machine can fix.'),
    dict(key='11-act-1-3', kind='console', title="Act One — The shop's server image, before any fix",
         body='ONE. (continued)\n    HIGH     ssh-root-login      /etc/ssh/sshd_config\n    HIGH     world-writable-dir  /var/www/uploads  auto\n    HIGH     world-writable-file /var/www/uploads/readme.txt  auto\n    MEDIUM   accepts-redirects   net.ipv4.conf.all.accept_redirects\n    MEDIUM   no-aslr             kernel.randomize_va_space\n    MEDIUM   ssh-passwords       /etc/ssh/sshd_config\n    LOW      no-syncookies       net.ipv4.tcp_syncookies\n    LOW      ssh-x11             /etc/ssh/sshd_config\n  THE COUNT:\n    severity  7 critical + 8 high + 3 medium + 2 low = 20\n    machine   7 auto, all of them file permissions\n    person    13 = 3 accounts + 4 sshd + 3 kernel + 3 ports',
         narration='The rest: high, medium and low. [[slnc 400]] The count: seven critical, eight high, three medium and two low make twenty. [[slnc 300]] Seven are auto. [[slnc 300]] Thirteen are for a person: three accounts, four S S H settings, three kernel settings and three ports.'),
    dict(key='12-act-2-figure', kind='figure', title='How each new mode is made',
         body='fix_math',
         narration='Second demo: the fixes a machine can make. [[slnc 400]] On the left, each file and its mode before the fix. [[slnc 300]] In the middle, the bits that change. [[slnc 300]] On the right, the new mode. [[slnc 700]] Each digit is three bits: read is four, write is two, execute is one. [[slnc 300]] The hidden shell loses the set user id bit: four seven five five, minus four thousand, is zero seven five five. [[slnc 300]] The cron script loses group write: minus twenty. [[slnc 300]] The upload folder and its file lose write for others: minus two. [[slnc 700]] The secrets keep only what the policy allows. [[slnc 300]] The shadow file becomes zero six four zero. [[slnc 300]] The host key and the app config become zero six zero zero: only the owner can read them. [[slnc 300]] Seven changes, and thirteen findings are left.'),
    dict(key='13-act-2-1', kind='console', title='Act Two — The fixes a machine can make',
         body='TWO. The fixes a machine can make.\n  BEFORE THE FIX:\n    20 findings, 7 of them marked auto\n  HOW EACH NEW MODE IS MADE (- takes bits away, & keeps only):\n    /tmp/.hidden-shell            4755 - 4000 = 0755  no set-user-id\n    /etc/cron.daily/backup.sh     0775 - 0020 = 0755  no group write\n    /etc/shadow                   0644 & 0640 = 0640  policy 0640\n    /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key 0644 & 0600 = 0600  policy 0600\n    /opt/app/config.properties    0644 & 0600 = 0600  policy 0600\n    /var/www/uploads              0777 - 0002 = 0775  no other write\n    /var/www/uploads/readme.txt   0666 - 0002 = 0664  no other write',
         narration='Here is the output. [[slnc 400]] Before the fix: twenty findings, seven of them auto. [[slnc 300]] Then each new mode, worked out. [[slnc 300]] A minus sign takes bits away. [[slnc 300]] An and sign keeps only the bits the policy allows.'),
    dict(key='14-act-2-2', kind='console', title='Act Two — The fixes a machine can make',
         body='TWO. (continued)\n  AFTER THE FIX:\n    changes    7\n    findings   20 - 7 = 13, none of them a permission\n    run again  0 changes: nothing left to fix',
         narration='After the fix: seven changes. [[slnc 300]] Twenty minus seven leaves thirteen findings, and none of them is a permission. [[slnc 300]] Run the fixer again, and it changes nothing.'),
    dict(key='15-act-3-figure', kind='figure', title='Reading an account line, and the port table in hex',
         body='port_decode',
         narration="Third demo: the decisions a person makes. [[slnc 400]] First, how the checker read the findings. [[slnc 300]] An account line has seven fields, split by colons. [[slnc 300]] The third field is the user id. [[slnc 300]] Toor has user id zero, which is root's number, so toor is a second root. [[slnc 300]] In the shadow file, the second field is the password hash, and for test it is empty. [[slnc 700]] Below, the kernel's port table. [[slnc 300]] It writes each address and port in hex. [[slnc 300]] Zero zero one seven in hex is twenty three, telnet. [[slnc 300]] An address of all zeros means every interface. [[slnc 300]] Zero one zero zero zero zero seven F, read backwards, is one two seven dot zero dot zero dot one: this host only. [[slnc 700]] So the person deletes two accounts, changes four S S H settings and three kernel settings, and stops three services."),
    dict(key='16-act-3-1', kind='console', title='Act Three — The decisions a person makes',
         body="THREE. The decisions a person makes.\n  HOW THE ACCOUNT LINES ARE READ (/etc/passwd, /etc/shadow):\n    toor:x:0:0:backdoor:/root:/bin/bash\n      name toor, UID 0 = root's number -> a second root\n    test::19000:0:99999:7:::\n      name test, password field empty -> no password\n  HOW THE PORT TABLE IS READ (/proc/net/tcp, hex):\n    00000000:0016  0.0.0.0    0x0016 = 22    allowed\n    00000000:0017  0.0.0.0    0x0017 = 23    not allowed\n    00000000:18EB  0.0.0.0    0x18EB = 6379  not allowed\n    0100007F:0CEA  127.0.0.1  0x0CEA = 3306  this host only\n    00000000:01BB  0.0.0.0    0x01BB = 443   allowed\n    00000000:0947  0.0.0.0    0x0947 = 2375  not allowed",
         narration='Here is the output. [[slnc 400]] The account lines, field by field: toor has user id zero, and test has an empty password field. [[slnc 300]] Then the port table, from hex to a number, with a verdict for each port.'),
    dict(key='17-act-3-2', kind='console', title='Act Three — The decisions a person makes',
         body='THREE. (continued)\n  BEFORE THE DECISIONS (13 findings):\n    login accounts          root, toor, test, ana\n    PermitRootLogin         yes\n    PasswordAuthentication  yes\n    PermitEmptyPasswords    yes\n    X11Forwarding           yes\n    randomize_va_space      0\n    tcp_syncookies          (unset)\n    accept_redirects        1\n    ports, every interface  22 23 443 2375 6379',
         narration='Before the decisions: thirteen findings. [[slnc 300]] Four login accounts, four S S H settings that say yes, kernel settings that are off or missing, and five ports open on every interface.'),
